# The status bar counts as Typora does: words in each block as its page
# holds them (markup and link addresses included), the markdown's
# characters and lines, and reading time rounded, "≤ 1 Minute" under a
# minute. While part of the document is selected, the count is the
# selection's of the whole, and the count menu lists the totals and the
# selection's words and characters; a total's row puts it in the bar.
type Some **bold** words, a [link](https://omarchy.org) here\none two
wait 300
check model.words === 10
check footer.countText(0) === "10 Words" && footer.countText(3) === "≤ 1 Minute"
check footer.countText(1) === model.characters + " Characters" && model.characters === model.sourceText().length
check footer.countText(2) === model.lines + " Lines" && model.lines === model.sourceText().split("\n").length
drag 1 0 1 7
wait 300
check footer.selWords === 2 && footer.selChars === 7
check footer.countText(0) === "2 / 10 Words" && footer.countText(1) === "7 / " + model.characters + " Characters"
clickItem footer.wordCount
wait 300
check footer.countMenu.visible && footer.countRows.count === 4
shot @SHOT@
clickItem footer.countRows.itemAt(3)
wait 200
check !footer.countMenu.visible && Prefs.countMode === 1
eval Prefs.countMode = 0
key Escape
dump @OUT@
